#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:13
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:16
msgid "**Linux OS**: Don't forget to install :ref:`platformio_udev_rules`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Windows OS**: Please check that you have correctly installed the USB "
"driver from the board manufacturer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:21
msgid ""
"If you find any issues with PlatformIO Core Installer Script, please report "
"to https://github.com/platformio/platformio-core-installer/issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:28
msgid "Multiple PlatformIO Cores in a system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:30
msgid ""
"Multiple standalone :ref:`piocore` in a system could lead to the different "
"issues. We highly recommend to keep one instance of PlatformIO Core or use "
"built-in PlatformIO Core in :ref:`pioide`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:34
msgid ""
":ref:`ide_vscode` - :ref:`ide_vscode_settings` > Set ``platformio-ide."
"useBuiltinPIOCore`` to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:36
msgid ""
"Finally, if you have a standalone :ref:`piocore` in a system, please open "
"system Terminal (not PlatformIO IDE Terminal) and uninstall obsolete "
"PlatformIO Core:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:47
msgid ""
"If you need to have :ref:`piocore` globally in a system, please :ref:"
"`piocore_install_shell_commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:51
msgid "'platformio' is not recognized as an internal or external command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:53
msgid ""
"If you use :ref:`pioide`, please check in PlatformIO IDE Settings that \"Use "
"built-in PlatformIO Core\" is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:56
msgid ""
"If you modify the system environment variable ``PATH`` in your Bash/Fish/ZSH "
"profile, please do not override global ``PATH``. This line ``export PATH=\"/"
"my/custom/path\"`` is incorrect. Use ``export PATH=\"/my/custom/path\":"
"$PATH`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:62
msgid "ImportError: cannot import name _remove_dead_weakref"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:64
msgid ""
"Windows users can experience this issue when multiple Python interpreters "
"are installed in a system and conflict with each other. The easy way to fix "
"this problem is uninstalling all Python interpreters using Windows Programs "
"Manager and installing them manually again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:69
msgid ""
"\"Windows > Start Menu > Settings > System > Apps & Features\", select "
"Python interpreters and uninstall them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:71
msgid ""
"Install the latest Python interpreter, see :ref:`faq_install_python` guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:72
msgid ""
"Remove ``C:\\Users\\YourUserName\\.platformio`` and ``C:\\.platformio`` "
"folders if exist (do not forget to replace \"YourUserName\" with the real "
"user name)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/installation/troubleshooting.rst:74
msgid "Restart :ref:`pioide`."
msgstr ""
